# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv/

# Tests, coverage and linter caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Environment: real values live in .env, and .env.example is the template
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Verity — everything the tooling generates. A new machine runs the setup
# anyway, so none of this belongs in history: committing it would pin a stale
# copy of a tool that is meant to stay on its latest version. VERITY.md is the
# deliberate exception — it is written by hand, not generated, and records the
# workarounds nothing else reproduces (including how to restore all of this).
#
# .verity/ also accumulates state that must never be committed: .snapshot/
# holds byte-for-byte copies of analyzed files, including any secret the gate
# just flagged.
# Verity installs itself into three harnesses, not one: Claude Code (.claude/),
# the AGENTS.md convention (.agents/) and Codex (.codex/). The skills and hook
# wiring are the same files in each.
#
# The one exception in .verity/ is standard.yaml, the shared Standard, which is meant
# to be committed. The knowledge graph under .verity/memory/ is machine-local too: the
# service rebuilds it, and committing it puts generated notes in every diff and pull
# request.
.verity/*
!.verity/standard.yaml
.codacy/
.claude/skills/verity-*/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.agents/skills/verity-*/
.codex/hooks.json
.codex/config.toml

# Ignore vscode AI rules
.github/instructions/codacy.instructions.md
